1. Project Overview\
\
The Hospital Management System is designed to organize and manage basic hospital operations. It helps manage patient information, doctor information, appointments, and medical records.\
\
2. Problem Statement\
\
Hospitals need an organized way to manage patient information, doctor details, appointments, and medical records. Managing these activities manually can lead to errors, delays, and difficulty accessing information.\
\
3. Project Purpose\
\
The purpose of this project is to design a Hospital Management System using UML Class Diagrams. The system represents the main classes, their attributes, methods, and relationships.\
\
4. Project Scope\
\
The project focuses on four main classes: Patient, Doctor, Appointment, and MedicalRecord. It models patient registration, doctor information, appointment scheduling, and medical record management.\
\
5. Project Objectives\
\
- Organize patient information.\
- Manage doctor details.\
- Schedule and cancel appointments.\
- Maintain medical records.\
- Represent system structure using a UML Class Diagram.\
\
6. Project Classes\
\
Patient\
\
Attributes: patientID, name, age, phone\
Methods: registerPatient(), updateDetails()\
\
Doctor\
\
Attributes: doctorID, name, specialization, phone\
Methods: viewAppointments(), updateDetails()\
\
Appointment\
\
Attributes: appointmentID, date, time, status\
Methods: scheduleAppointment(), cancelAppointment()\
\
MedicalRecord\
\
Attributes: recordID, diagnosis, treatment\
Methods: addRecord(), updateRecord()\
\
7. Relationships Between Classes\
\
- One Patient can have multiple Appointments.\
- One Doctor can have multiple Appointments.\
- In this simplified project model, one Patient is associated with one MedicalRecord.\
\
8. Conclusion\
\
The Hospital Management System demonstrates how UML Class Diagrams can represent the structure of a software system. The diagram identifies the main classes, their attributes, methods, and relationships.}